---
import { themes,heritage } from '../../../src/palettes.mjs';
import { contrastRatio } from '../../../src/contrast.mjs';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { version } from '../../../package.json';
import ThemeSpecimen from '../components/ThemeSpecimen.astro';
const entries=Object.values(themes);
const origins=[['Silver',heritage.silver],['Light blue',heritage.blueLight],['Blue',heritage.blue],['Dark blue',heritage.blueDark],['Gold',heritage.gold],['Dark gold',heritage.goldDark],['Light yellow',heritage.yellowLight]];
const pairs=Object.entries(themes.light.tokens);
const colors=pairs.filter(([,value])=>/^#[a-f\d]{6}$/i.test(value));
const category=(key)=>key.startsWith('syntax-')?'syntax':key.startsWith('chart-')?'charts':/^(info|success|warning|danger|error|green)/.test(key)?'status':'interface';
const downloads=[['CSS variables','Scoped Light and Dark themes','martlet.css'],['JSON tokens','The complete color specification','martlet.json'],['Light CSS','Light theme on its own','martlet-light.css'],['Dark CSS','Dark theme on its own','martlet-dark.css'],['VS Code Light','Starter color definition','martlet-light-vscode.json'],['VS Code Dark','Starter color definition','martlet-dark-vscode.json'],['Terminal Light JSON','Sixteen ANSI colors','martlet-light-terminal.json'],['Terminal Dark JSON','Sixteen ANSI colors','martlet-dark-terminal.json']];
---
<BaseLayout>
  <div class="specimen-book">
    <header class="book-intro">
      <div class="book-title"><h1>Martlet<span>.</span></h1><p>Color with a story.</p></div>
      <div class="book-description"><p>Blue and silver in the light. Navy and gold in the dark. A pair of color themes for interfaces, readable code, and the terminal you keep open all day.</p><div class="intro-links"><a href="#downloads">Get Martlet <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a href="#story">Where it began <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><span>v{version}</span></div></div>
    </header>

    <section id="preview" aria-label="Compare Martlet Light and Dark">
      <div class="specimen-toolbar"><p>One palette family. Two ways to work.</p><div class="view-switch" role="group" aria-label="Example type"><button type="button" data-example="interface" aria-pressed="true">Interface</button><button type="button" data-example="code" aria-pressed="false">Code</button><button type="button" data-example="terminal" aria-pressed="false">Terminal</button></div></div>
      <div class="specimen-spread">{entries.map(theme=><ThemeSpecimen theme={theme}/>)}</div>
      <p class="caption">Illustrative examples using the actual Martlet colors. Select a swatch to copy its hex value.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="palette" class="palette-workspace" aria-labelledby="palette-title">
      <header class="workspace-heading"><div><h2 id="palette-title">Find your colors.</h2><p>Every role has a name. Every value is ready to copy.</p></div><div class="mode-switch" role="group" aria-label="Palette appearance"><button type="button" data-palette-mode="light" aria-pressed="true">Light palette</button><button type="button" data-palette-mode="dark" aria-pressed="false">Dark palette</button></div></header>
      <div class="workspace-columns">
        <div id="tokens" class="token-reference">
          <div class="token-filters"><label>Find a token<input id="token-search" type="search" placeholder="Try accent, syntax, or border" autocomplete="off" /></label><label>Show<select id="token-category"><option value="all">All roles</option><option value="interface">Interface</option><option value="status">Status</option><option value="syntax">Syntax</option><option value="charts">Charts</option></select></label></div>
          <p id="token-count" class="reference-count" role="status">{pairs.length} tokens · Light palette</p>
          <div class="token-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Color token reference" tabindex="0">
            <table class="token-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Value</th><th scope="col"><span class="sr-only">Copy value</span></th></tr></thead><tbody>{pairs.map(([key,value])=><tr data-token={key} data-category={category(key)} data-light={value} data-dark={themes.dark.tokens[key]}><th scope="row"><span class="token-color" style={key==='shadow'?`box-shadow:${value}`:`background:${value}`}></span><code>{key}</code></th><td class="token-value"><code>{value}</code></td><td><button class="copy-token" type="button" data-copy={value} aria-label={`Copy ${key} ${value}`}>Copy</button></td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
          </div>
          <p id="no-tokens" class="empty-result" hidden>No matching tokens. Try another name or category.</p>
          <p class="caption">CSS names use the prefix <code>--martlet-</code>. Shadow and translucent colors are included in the reference.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="contrast-inspector" aria-labelledby="contrast-title">
          <h3 id="contrast-title">Put two colors together.</h3><p>Check a foreground against a background before you use it.</p>
          <div class="contrast-controls"><label>Foreground<select id="contrast-foreground">{colors.map(([key])=><option value={key} selected={key==='text'}>{key}</option>)}</select></label><label>Background<select id="contrast-background">{colors.map(([key])=><option value={key} selected={key==='bg'}>{key}</option>)}</select></label></div>
          <div id="contrast-sample" class="contrast-sample" style={`background:${themes.light.tokens.bg};color:${themes.light.tokens.text}`}><span>Aa</span><p>A little room to think.<br />A clear place to begin.</p></div>
          <div class="contrast-result" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"><strong id="contrast-ratio">{contrastRatio(themes.light.tokens.text,themes.light.tokens.bg).toFixed(2)}:1</strong><span id="contrast-verdict">AA and AAA for normal text</span></div>
          <p class="caption">WCAG 2 contrast for the selected opaque sRGB colors. A passing pair does not establish accessibility for a whole application.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="downloads" class="get-martlet" aria-labelledby="download-title">
      <header class="workspace-heading"><div><h2 id="download-title">Take Martlet with you.</h2><p>Pick a format. The same source colors go with it.</p></div><a class="source-link" href="https://github.com/k3jph/martlettheme">Browse the source ↗</a></header>
      <div class="installation-grid">
        <article class="terminal-download"><div class="terminal-symbol" aria-hidden="true">&gt;_</div><h3>Terminal.app</h3><p>Native profiles for the terminal included with macOS. Background, text, cursor, selection, and all sixteen ANSI colors.</p><div class="terminal-download-links"><a href="/downloads/martlet-light.terminal" download>Martlet Light <span>↓ .terminal</span></a><a href="/downloads/martlet-dark.terminal" download>Martlet Dark <span>↓ .terminal</span></a></div><details><summary>How to install</summary><ol><li>Download either profile.</li><li>Open Terminal and choose <strong>Terminal → Settings → Profiles</strong>.</li><li>Use the action menu beneath the profiles list to choose <strong>Import</strong>, then select the downloaded file. You can also drag the file into that list.</li><li>Select Martlet Light or Martlet Dark. Choose <strong>Default</strong> if you want it for new windows.</li></ol><p><a href="https://support.apple.com/guide/terminal/import-and-export-terminal-profiles-trml4299c696/mac">Apple’s profile import guide ↗</a></p><p>These profiles have not yet been tested in Terminal.app on a Mac.</p></details></article>
        <div class="download-list">{downloads.map(([title,description,file])=><a href={`/downloads/${file}`} download><span><strong>{title}</strong><small>{description}</small></span><code>{file.endsWith('.css')?'.css':'.json'} ↓</code></a>)}</div>
      </div>
      <details class="css-instructions"><summary>Use Martlet on a website</summary><p>Load the CSS, then set <code>data-martlet</code> to <code>light</code> or <code>dark</code> on the element you want to theme.</p><pre><code>&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="martlet.css"&gt;
&lt;main data-martlet="dark"&gt;
  &lt;article class="panel"&gt;Hello, Martlet.&lt;/article&gt;
&lt;/main&gt;

.panel &#123;
  background: var(--martlet-panel);
  color: var(--martlet-text);
&#125;</code></pre><p>Light and Dark can also live in separate parts of the same page, as they do here. The VS Code files are starter color definitions; they are not packaged extensions.</p></details>
    </section>

    <section id="story" class="origin-story" aria-labelledby="story-title">
      <div class="origin-mark"><img src="/martlet-mark.svg" width="160" height="160" alt="A gold martlet on blue" loading="lazy"/><span>Blue. Silver. Gold.</span></div>
      <div class="origin-prose"><h2 id="story-title">A personal beginning.</h2><p>Martlet begins with the blue, silver, and gold of James P. Howard, II’s personal heraldic identity and the <a href="https://jameshoward.us/2025/05/26/a-new-tartan/">James Howard &amp; Family tartan</a>. Those are the colors of one family’s identity. The martlet gives the theme its name and its mark.</p><p>The first Light and Dark themes were built for <a href="https://prism7.app/">Prism 7</a>. This independent project extends them to interfaces, source code, and terminals. Light gives blue the leading role; Dark brings gold forward against navy. The surfaces, text colors, and supporting hues are practical additions, adjusted for the work each color has to do.</p><p>The original seven colors remain the source references shown below. The application colors can develop as Martlet is tested in more places.</p></div>
      <div class="heritage-strip">{origins.map(([name,hex])=><button type="button" data-copy={hex} aria-label={`Copy original ${name.toLowerCase()} ${hex}`}><span style={`background:${hex}`}></span><strong>{name}</strong><code>{hex}</code></button>)}</div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <p id="copy-status" class="copy-feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  <dialog id="copy-dialog" class="copy-dialog" aria-labelledby="copy-title"><h2 id="copy-title">Copy this value</h2><p>Clipboard access is unavailable. Select the value below and copy it.</p><label>Color value<input id="copy-value" readonly /></label><button type="button" data-copy-close>Close</button></dialog>
  <script src="../scripts/specimen.js"></script>
</BaseLayout>
